<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sena, Mozambique</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sena is a town on the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. Already a trading post of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili merchants</a>, it was occupied by the Portuguese in the 1530s and became, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tete">Tete</a> upriver, one of their main bases in the interior, trading with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> state and the Barwe kingdom and serving as a centre of the prazo estates. A railway bridge across the Zambezi there was opened in 1935.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sena-mozambique.jpg" alt="Sena, Mozambique" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hajo42 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beira-Moatize_21.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
